wildos-settings (0.1.25) trixie; urgency=medium

  * System > Recovery: restore points with Go back, Create a restore
    point, how many are kept and how much space they use, Reset Wild OS,
    Start-up options and Back up your files.
  * Going back says what goes back and what stays as it is, can hold the
    update back for two weeks, and restarts once. Today's version is
    saved as a restore point too.
  * Updates has Go back beside What's new on the latest Wild OS build.
  * Reset Wild OS is shown and arrives in an update.
  * Back up your files opens Backup and says when it last ran.
  * The graphics driver's restore point is named after the driver.

