wildos-settings (0.1.15) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Accounts > Sign-in options is laid out as the design has it: Ways to
    sign in (Fingerprint, Password with when it last changed, Security
    key), then "Use your fingerprint for", with switches for signing in
    and unlocking and for admin prompts, and the disk at start-up on the
    password only. With no reader the fingerprint parts are left out, and
    they appear when a reader is plugged in.
  * Setting up a fingerprint is one dialog in four steps: your password,
    touches in the middle of the finger, then the edges, then done. A
    ring and the print fill as the reader takes each touch, and a touch
    that doesn't count says why without losing your place. Add another
    finger straight after, or manage and remove them later.
  * Security key is listed, but Wild OS can't sign in with one yet, and
    says so.
  * About lists Fluent UI System Icons, whose fingerprint the setup uses.

 -- Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>  Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:00:00 +0000

